  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "The unit everything is priced against",
   "items": [
    "A token is whatever the tokenizer cut the string into \u2014 not a word, not a character",
    "Token counts are not proportional to character or word counts in any fixed way",
    "Cost and capacity are counted in tokens, never in words"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "title": "What the KV cache remembers",
   "items": [
    "Every past token contributes one K and one V per layer, per head",
    "The cache avoids re-deriving the prefix on each decode step",
    "Cache memory scales with sequence length (arithmetic in Ch. 7)"
